Boost 1.84.0: let Boost.Asio configure without Boost.Context/Boost.Coroutine.

Why: Boost.Context has only per-architecture assembly (no wasm32 backend), so we exclude it
(and Coroutine, which needs it). Asio's generated CMake still links both, which makes the whole
Boost configure fail. Asio itself is header-only and only needs Context for asio::spawn, which
libslic3r never uses (its only Asio/Beast use is beast/core/detail/base64.hpp).
Upstreamable: no (wasm-specific). Applies with: patch -p1
--- a/libs/asio/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libs/asio/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -17,8 +17,6 @@
     Boost::align
     Boost::assert
     Boost::config
-    Boost::context
-    Boost::coroutine
     Boost::date_time
     Boost::system
     Boost::throw_exception
